    "case_id": "567",
    "case_summary": "A 59-year-old immunocompromised man with a history of duodenal adenocarcinoma receiving palliative gemcitabine and paclitaxel presented for evaluation of bicytopenia. The patient developed progressive renal failure with microscopic hematuria. He was on prophylactic penicillin, to which he was adherent. Ten days later, the patient returned with fatigue and chills.\n\nPatient was afebrile, hypertensive to 185/104 mm Hg, and tachycardic to 122 beats/min. He appeared fatigued. Examination was otherwise unremarkable, without evidence of meningismus, rash, joint abnormalities, or genitourinary symptoms.\n\n- Laboratory findings:    * Leukocytosis to 22.4×10⁹/L    * Lactatemia to 2.5 mmol/L    * Serum creatinine level of 312.1 μmol/L (3.53 mg/dL; baseline, 171.5 μmol/L [1.94 mg/dL])    * Peripheral blood cultures: 2/2 cultures grew Gram-negative cocci    - Microbiology:    * Blood culture speciation results positive",
